# OAuth URL Scheme Handling Fix

## Problem
OAuth callback from Google was opening a new app instance instead of routing to the existing running instance on macOS.

## Root Cause
macOS Launch Services was launching a new instance because:
1. Missing `LSApplicationCategoryType` in Info.plist
2. App wasn't properly bringing itself to foreground on URL receipt
3. Launch Services didn't recognize the app as capable of handling URLs while running

## Solution
1. **Added LSApplicationCategoryType**: Set to `public.app-category.productivity` in Info.plist
2. **Enhanced URL Handler**: Modified `handleOAuthCallback` to activate app and bring window to front
3. **Proper Window Management**: Ensured main window becomes key when OAuth callback received

## Code Changes
- Info.plist: Added `<key>LSApplicationCategoryType</key><string>public.app-category.productivity</string>`
- MacAppDelegate.handleOAuthCallback: Added `NSApplication.shared.activate(ignoringOtherApps: true)` and window activation

## Result
OAuth callbacks now properly route to existing app instance, preventing duplicate initialization and maintaining user session context.